  "text": "Using the fact that the area of the pool is \n120\n square feet, it can be shown that the value of \n𝑥\n is given by one of the roots of the polynomial\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\n𝑥\n3\n+\n𝑥\n2\n−\n3\n600.\nWhich of the above diagrams could be the graph of \n𝑦\n=\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n?\n Enter \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", or \"D\" (without quotes).\nThe diagram which shows \n𝑦\n=\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n is \nD .\n\tCorrect\nExplanation\n\nLet's analyze the given polynomial:\n\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\n𝑥\n3\n+\n𝑥\n2\n−\n3\n600\n\nThe degree (\n𝑛\n=\n3\n) is odd, and the leading coefficient (\n𝑎\n3\n=\n1\n) is positive. Therefore, the polynomial has the following end behavior:\n\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n→\n−\n∞\n as \n𝑥\n→\n−\n∞\n.\n\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n→\n∞\n as \n𝑥\n→\n∞\n.\n\nOnly the graph \n𝐷\n satisfies these conditions."
}